# A burial [[shroud]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} A collection of [[tallow]] rising up against the [[wick]] of a [[candle]], once regarded as an [[omen]] of [[death]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1859|author=Charles Dickens|title=A Tale of Two Cities|passage=He resorted to his pint of wine for consolation, drank it all in a few minutes, and fell asleep on his arms, with his hair straggling over the table, and a long '''winding-sheet''' in the candle dripping down upon him.}}

